From db9e1ae96e895a6cc0119c2ee113e4e852a41ea2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 11:30:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 188/194] glm: TF_GLM_KV_SPLIT on 8-bit rows; exact decode
 windows (the picks' union gathered, the unchanged attention); host tests

Decode windows past the dense prefix gather the union of their picks from the ranks that hold them and run
dsa_block's sparse attention on those rows with the lists remapped: bit-identical to unsplit. Windows in the
prefix take the prompt path. TF_GLM_KV_SPLIT_DECODE=lse keeps the query-gather path (BF16, not exact).
Int8 and E4M3 rows: codes and scales gathered and kept apart. test-glm-kv-split-host runs the module's tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UQVvNktFCvQrvpNUbqtqBX
